jg@cs.brown.edu (Jeremy Gaffney) writes:

>Actually, my _main_ goals for these lower levels is to find FOOD absolutely
>ASAP - I've had more trouble with wizards and starvation than any other class,
>probably because I have to run so much...:)

You might be having trouble with wizards in particular because they start
with two rings.  Some rings drastically increase food consumption, like a ring
of regeneration.  Therefore, it is wise to remove such rings when they are
not needed... ie, remove a ring of regeneration when you are at full health,
and put it on just before battle.

To be honest, I've never had enough problems with food to be very concerned
about it.  Sure, I pile up food rations on each level as I find them, but I
don't plan to go "food hunting" from the start.

Oh yeah, I just realized why I don't have food problems.... (duh)

SPOILERS

You start with a diety, so use it.  When you become hungry, wait another 50
or so turns (actually, until you become weak) and pray.  Your stomach will
always feel content provided the proper prayer conditions are met.  (luck,
happy god, etc.)

You start the game with all the right conditions and if you don't screw
them up, food will never be a problem.  Occasionally (with heavy use of a
ring) you will become weak and or faint before the prayer time out has
expired.   You should know when this is the case, and only then will you
need to actually eat.
